    "durationMs": 239444,
    "finalText": "Implementation complete. The URL shortener is fully built and verified:\n\n- **Stack**: axum 0.8.4 + SQLx 0.8 (Postgres) + tokio, reading `DATABASE_URL` from the environment (nothing hard-coded).\n- **Persistence**: `migrations/0001_create_links.sql` creates the `links` table (unique `code`, `clicks` counter); `sqlx::migrate!()` applies pending migrations at startup, before the listener binds — data and click counts survive restarts (verified: a link with 4 clicks survived a kill/restart cycle).\n- **Endpoints**: `POST /links` (201 with `{\"code\",\"url\",\"clicks\":0}`, URL returned byte-for-byte unchanged; duplicate custom code → 409; auto-generated 8-char codes on omission), `GET /links/{code}` (200/404), `GET /r/{code}` (302 with exact `Location`, atomic single-statement `clicks = clicks + 1`), `GET /links` (ascending creation order with `total`).\n- **Validation**: URL parsed with the `url` crate (must be absolute http/https with a host); codes validated as 4–20 chars of `[A-Za-z0-9_-]` (boundaries tested at 3/4/19/20/21); malformed JSON, missing/invalid url, and invalid codes all return 422 JSON with an `error` field via manual body parsing.\n- **`start.sh`**: runs the already-built release binary in the foreground on `0.0.0.0:8000` after migrations; README documents startup.\n\nAll ~40 test assertions passed, including the restart-persistence check. The test server has been stopped, so port 8000 is free for the automated suite."
  }
